# oracle: velocity all create, then velocity half zero angular on the 54 atoms with id <= 54 of a 3d LJ fcc block (108 atoms): a non-singular inertia tensor, so Group::omega takes the inverse path (det > EPSILON, src/group.cpp at b332f28), then 10 NVE steps
# native: b332f28 installed lmp (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp), no extra package
# measured: (filled in by the run)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units          lj
dimension      3
boundary       p p p
atom_style     atomic
lattice        fcc 0.8442
region         box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box     1 box
create_atoms   1 box
mass           * 1.0
velocity       all create 1.44 87287 loop geom
group          half id <= 54
velocity       half zero angular
pair_style     lj/cut 2.5
pair_coeff     * * 1.0 1.0 2.5
fix            1 all nve
thermo_style   custom step temp pe ke
thermo_modify  format float %.15g
thermo         5
run            10
